cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use APS in research or teaching, cite this repository and identify the commit or recorded evidence revision you used."
type: software
title: "Agentic Process Safety (APS)"
authors:
  - name: "SafetyMP"
    website: "https://github.com/SafetyMP"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SafetyMP/Agentic-Process-Safety"
url: "https://safetymp.github.io/Agentic-Process-Safety/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  An open-source research sandbox for investigating agent workflow hazards
  through same-request control comparisons, case-specific causal paths,
  recorded synthetic evidence and human reasoning. APS includes a static
  guided investigation app and a separate HAZOP-inspired Python/OPA research
  implementation. Illustrative outcomes and finite experiments do not
  establish operational safety or the superiority of an analysis method.
keywords:
  - agentic process safety
  - multi-agent systems
  - hazard analysis
  - HAZOP
  - agent governance
  - human reasoning
